#: ../../source/pipeline_README.md:77
msgid ""
"This means a message *m2* can be pushed into a session while it's still "
"processing the preceding message *m1*. The messages can be processed "
"concurrently but they *must* be given to the next session in line (or to "
"the application) in the same order they came in. Applications will expect"
" to receive messages in the order they arrived over the wire, and "
"sessions require this too. So ordering of messages must be preserved "
"throughout the pipeline."
msgstr ""

